WEBVTT

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:08.000
<i>The summer of our third 
year of middle school.</i>

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.740
<i>Back then, if we were anxious 
about anything in our future,</i>

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.130
<i>it would have been our high school 
entrance exams, and not much else.</i>

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:18.730
<i>But, they were such a small thing.</i>

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.260
<i>Since starting surfing, 
every day shone brightly.</i>

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:30.090
<i>The future overflowed 
with that same sort of light.</i>

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.150
<i>That's what we believed.</i>

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:35.220
<i>When I think back on it now,</i>

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:39.260
<i>the time I spent with those incomparable 
friends was so very precious...</i>

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.250
<i>Every day was miraculous.</i>

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:46.650
<b>Sweet
Dried 
Sweet 
Potato</b>

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.650
Finally, it's next week.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.360
Yes, it is.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.220
The Forest Cup!

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.910
Our chance to make memories!

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.310
Listen up, Sho, Tanaka!

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:07.590
I will show you the culmination 
of my life of surfing!

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:10.230
Something you'll never forget 
for as long as you live!

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:12.190
You say "culmination," but...

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:16.250
It's only been a year 
since Corgi started surfing.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:17.950
No one asked you, Murphy!

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:20.680
Even if it's only been a year, 
the culmination is the culmination!

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.180
But, Masaki, you've really 
gotten good in just a year.

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:25.640
Right?

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:28.190
Right! We're aiming for victory!

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:31.190
You're making too much of yourself!

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:51.880
Let's Go Surfing!!

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:10.660
3rd Wave First Competition

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.040
<b>Aim for Victory!!</b>

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.050
This Kosuke guy...

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:21.050
The way he turns his board to match the 
break of the wave... his timing's perfect.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:28.060
At the competition, I'm going to nail 
my off the lip just like this guy!

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:31.090
Okay! Time for some image training!

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.490
What do you think?

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.090
Yay!

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:04.590
<i>Everyone, welcome to the Forest 
Cup at Oarai Sun Beach.</i>

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:08.600
<i>I am the chair of the competition's 
executive committee, Mori William Soichiro.</i>

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:11.730
The chair of the executive committee 
is really young, isn't he?

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:11.510
<i>Today, the weather has decided to favor us.</i>

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:13.150
<i>It's a perfect day for surfing.</i>

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.150
I heard he's around our age.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:14.630
Seriously? That's crazy!

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:18.890
<i>Let's try to be careful of injury 
and enjoy the waves of Oarai together.</i>

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:16.790
They say he's the son of a billionaire,

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:18.890
and he's got a thousand 
surfboards in his collection.

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:20.360
<i>This Forest—</i>

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:20.360
A thousand?

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.290
Oops...

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:27.370
<i>This Forest Cup is held 
in many different places.</i>

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.890
<i>In addition to popularizing surfing,</i>

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:33.870
<i>we aim to discover young stars 
no one's seen before.</i>

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.680
<i>Now, I'd like to begin the competition.</i>

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:37.910
<i>To good waves!</i>

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.790
To good waves!

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:43.560
I'm in round 1, heat 2.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.380
I'm in heat 3.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.040
That means I'd be up against 
Sho in the semifinals, right?

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.670
Only if you manage to win enough 
to get that far, Corgi.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:54.390
I will win my way there! 
Because I'm aiming for victory!

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:56.470
Huh?

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.670
What character is that?

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:02.900
Dunno.

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:06.910
It's Magical Maid Miruru.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:09.750
You don't even know Miruru?

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.290
This is why surfers are just so...

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.920
"Miruru"... he said.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.110
That thing is actually pretty cute.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:22.190
Masaki. Setting Miruru aside, 
how are you on the rules?

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:23.230
Do you have them covered?

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:24.290
Yeah!

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:30.180
<i>Now for Round 1, heat 1. 
Kido Naoya and Fukutome Daigo.</i>

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.310
<i>The time limit is 30 minutes.</i>

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:34.830
<i>Now, start the heat!</i>

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:37.810
<i>First, they're both heading out 
to try to get wave priority.</i>

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:41.440
This is going by man-on-man priority rules.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:46.450
The one who makes it out the fastest gains 
the right to catch waves first, right?

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:49.600
That's right. That's what 
"priority" means here.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.720
Vewy good! Aw, you're doing so well!

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.600
Don't treat me like a child!

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:58.130
<i>Kido has gained priority!</i>

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:00.580
<i>Now we wait for a good wave!</i>

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:03.720
If you don't pick a wave with a nice break,

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:08.060
it's hard to rack up points, 
no matter how skilled you are.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.080
The moment has come!

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:20.850
Raven-Dark Blue Angel...

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:22.520
descend!

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:28.040
<i>Just look at Kido! High points 
starting with his first run!</i>

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:31.950
Wow. He flew pretty high.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.510
And his landing was solid.

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:36.220
And he shouted a super-cool
 name for his move!

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:37.370
Was it cool?

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.880
I didn't quite understand 
the name of that move,

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:41.200
but he's very good, isn't he?

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.740
Well, he is good enough to be 
in this competition, after all.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:46.980
Hello, Shoko-san! Uncle!

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:48.500
Hello!

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:49.510
Where is he?

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:51.420
He's at work today, as usual.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:54.820
So, we need to cheer on Masaki 
for his dad's sake, too!

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:57.140
Sakura and I made this together.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:00.020
<b>Masaki

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:58.040
Here you are.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.670
When is Masaki-kun's heat?

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:04.020
It's the next one. 
I just hope he doesn't drown.

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:11.110
<i>In heat 1, the winner is Kido Naoya.</i>

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:13.030
<i>Next up, heat 2.</i>

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:16.540
<i>Hinaoka Masaki and Shimada Shunichiro.</i>

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:23.270
Come on, Corgi. You're up!

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:33.050
Okay. Let's do this!

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:41.300
<i>Oh, man... I'm starting 
to get kinda nervous.</i>

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:44.620
Masaki.

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:45.770
Masaki!

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:50.620
Masaki.

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:53.570
If you do what you always do 
in practice, you'll be fine.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:56.380
Like I practiced...

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:02.710
<i>Like this?</i>

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:04.740
<i>Yes, that's it!</i>

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:07.610
<i>The show must go on!</i>

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:09.090
<i>Masaki! You're going!</i>

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.620
<i>Hurry up and go!</i>

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:12.550
<i>Look ahead! Go faster!</i>

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:15.220
<i>I'm gonna practice more and more!</i>

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:17.600
<i>Surfing isn't that easy.</i>

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:19.760
<i>You have to practice over and over!</i>

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:21.230
<i>Take off!</i>

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.980
<i>Yahoo!</i>

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.650
<i>Sho! Tanaka! Did you see that just now?</i>

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:29.320
<i>Waiting for a good wave. 
Picking the right wave and riding it.</i>

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:30.730
<i>Just like Sho...</i>

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:32.680
<i>I told you not to push yourself too hard!</i>

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:35.230
<i>Surfing is so much fun...</i>

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:36.740
<i>My goal...</i>

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:40.130
<i>Tanaka and I are here. 
There's nothing for you to worry about.</i>

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:41.200
<i>Okay!</i>

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:44.300
<i>I will never forget that feeling.</i>

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:45.720
<i>That's true.</i>

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:47.500
<i>Let's go surfing!</i>

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.590
<i>Let's do that competition!</i>

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:51.000
Right.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:57.510
Let's go!

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:59.320
<i>Start the heat!</i>

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.010
<i>They're heading out!</i>

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:14.880
Masaki, you can do it!

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:21.160
<b>Masaki    Fight</b>

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:17.850
Go! Go! Masaki!

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:17.850
Mom, stop shouting so loud.

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:19.030
Huh? Why?

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.160
If I don't shout loud, he won't 
be able to hear me, right?

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.230
He won't hear no matter how loud you shout.

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:25.660
Masaki-kun's got priority.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:28.670
<i>Now, Hinaoka's gotten himself priority.</i>

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:31.670
<i>Forest Cup in Sun Beach...</i>

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:38.650
<i>That day I saw Sho...</i>

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.370
<i>It's been a year since then.</i>

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:43.660
<i>I said I wanted to be like Sho...</i>

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:46.350
<i>and I've been trying to catch up 
with him ever since.</i>

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:49.690
<i>Whether I've gotten any closer or not... 
we'll find that out today.</i>

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:53.410
<i>I'm going to do everything 
that's in my power to do!</i>

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:59.660
<i>Hinaoka seems to have let this one go.</i>

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:58.200
<i>No. Not yet.</i>

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.250
What's this? I thought he was 
going to go, but he didn't.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:03.080
Because it wasn't quite good enough.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:05.530
Guess he's all grown up now, 
choosing his waves like that.

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:08.580
That's it, Masaki. No need to rush.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:11.590
<i>Five minutes have passed 
and he still hasn't made his move.</i>

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:16.090
This is it!

00:10:16.390 --> 00:10:18.080
A good wave!

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:20.090
I'll ride this one!

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.600
<b>Masaki    Fight</b>

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:23.100
<i>Hinaoka has caught a wave!</i>

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:29.020
Now!

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:32.820
<i>An impressive sense of balance!</i>

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:36.610
<i>He takes a long line and delivers 
a beautiful off the lip!</i>

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:39.280
<i>We can expect some big points from this!</i>

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:40.250
Yes!

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:41.780
That was amazing, Masaki!

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.350
You're amazing, Big Brother!

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:57.030
Corgi!

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:57.030
Masaki!

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.440
H-How was I?

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:04.390
I couldn't hear whose points 
were higher way out there.

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:05.690
You won!

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:06.760
What?

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:09.560
You've advanced to round 2!

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:11.130
R-Really?

00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:14.070
What's wrong?

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:15.300
Masaki?

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.160
I...

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:17.680
I?

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:20.820
I... I did it...

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.830
I did it!

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:28.740
I did it! Yes! I did it! Yay! I won!

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:30.360
I did it! I did it!

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:35.650
<i>The joy of winning flooded my whole body.</i>

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:37.680
<i>Like a small child...</i>

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:40.700
<i>I was truly happy.</i>

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:42.820
<i>I was happy about winning, of course, but...</i>

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:45.850
<i>I felt like I hadn't spent 
the last year in vain...</i>

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:49.850
<i>Like the ocean was 
acknowledging me as a surfer.</i>

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:58.360
<i>Hinaoka made the most 
of the smallest of chances and won!</i>

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:22.850
<i>The heats in Round 1 continued.</i>

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:26.730
<i>Sho, of course, moved 
to Round 2, as did Tanaka.</i>

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:27.820
<i>Then...</i>

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:29.720
<i>Round 2, heat 1.</i>

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:32.910
<i>Kido Naoya and Hinaoka Masaki.</i>

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:35.910
<i>And Kido has taken priority!</i>

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:38.840
He's fast.

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:40.920
He doesn't have Miruru for nothing!

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:46.150
Say, Naoya!

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:47.120
Naoya?

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:50.940
The name of that move before. 
It was so cool! Like a finishing skill!

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:51.970
Really?

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:54.830
Thank you, um... Hinaoka.

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:56.430
You can call me Masaki.

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:59.190
Earlier, did you say you were going to win?

00:13:59.190 --> 00:13:59.940
Yeah!

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:02.440
Can't say I hate that kind of thing.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:03.400
Huh?

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:07.200
Well, I'll head out first.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:10.200
<i>Kido Naoya takes off!</i>

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:12.840
That cloud is calling...

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:17.350
Rend the darkness... Meteor Fantasista!

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:27.640
The names of his moves are so cool!

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:29.890
Whoops. This is no time to be impressed.

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:31.470
I need to deliver, too.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:34.470
Another off the lip, no, um...

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:37.590
The Oarai is Shining 
Thunder! I'm gonna nail it!

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:41.150
<i>Next, Hinaoka has caught a wave!</i>

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:46.770
<i>Oh, what a shame! 
He lost his balance and wiped out!</i>

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:46.770
Oh! He fell.

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:49.410
He was thinking about things he 
didn't need to be thinking about.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:52.760
<i>Next, it's Kido's turn.</i>

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:54.230
<i>This is bad. How many minutes are left?</i>

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:05.400
I can't hear them at all.

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:09.660
<i>But the next wave 
is probably my last chance.</i>

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:16.020
<i>Kido has started paddling.</i>

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:19.090
<i>What's this? Looks like he's 
caught another good wave!</i>

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:24.770
<i>A splendid aerial!</i>

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:28.030
<i>We can expect an even better score here!</i>

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:32.030
<i>Was that about 6 points?</i>

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:35.870
<i>For me to turn this around, 
I need at least 8 points!</i>

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.400
<i>This is no time to be saying 
stuff like, "Oarai Shining"!</i>

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:40.240
<i>I need to deliver a big trick!</i>

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:43.100
<i>I want to win again and celebrate...</i>

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:45.530
<i>I want that feeling again!</i>

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:51.300
<i>Okay! This is a good wave! 
And my timing is perfect!</i>

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:56.510
<i>But this isn't enough to turn things around.</i>

00:15:56.510 --> 00:15:58.310
<i>I'm going to deliver a floater!</i>

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:02.800
<i>This is bad!</i>

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:07.910
<i>That's too bad for Hinaoka!</i>

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:08.760
It's because he pushes himself too hard.

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:10.560
<i>So close on his second maneuver, 
but ending in failure!</i>

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:11.320
But his challenger's spirit is good.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:15.800
<i>Round 2, heat 1. Kido Naoya wins.</i>

00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:18.260
Big Brother...

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:21.780
He's fine. I think he just 
swallowed a little seawater is all.

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:23.830
I-It's not like I'm worried or anything!

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:27.230
The fact that he won even once 
is an amazing result for him!

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:30.950
Okay! Next, we cheer for Sho-sama!

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:32.340
Yes.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:35.840
<b>Sho-sama     Fight!</b>

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:34.020
Here you go.

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:44.990
<i>Round 2, heat 2.</i>

00:16:44.990 --> 00:16:48.510
<i>Akitsuki Sho and Matsukaze Yuta.</i>

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:49.260
I was supposed to go up against Sho.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:51.760
Victory?

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:53.860
I need to practice so much more!

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:57.080
I need to get so much better!

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:04.930
<i>He's been surfing for as long 
as he can remember.</i>

00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:07.610
<i>Born to surf, Matsukaze!</i>

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:10.380
<i>He controls the board like 
it's a part of his body!</i>

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:16.350
That felt good.

00:17:16.350 --> 00:17:20.080
According to the data, the chances 
of my winning this round are—

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:21.890
Huh?

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:24.890
<i>Akitsuki has caught a massive wave!</i>

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:27.900
<i>It's a thing of beauty!</i>

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:30.900
<i>No complaints, we're expecting 
some high scores for this!</i>

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:32.530
What did he say?

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:39.160
<i>Oops! I forgot the play-by-play.</i>

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:43.120
<i>But there's no mistake, 
Akitsuki should be getting a high score!</i>

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:41.910
Sho-sama!

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:43.120
Sho-kun!

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.410
Sho-sama!

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:47.280
That boy really is amazing, isn't he?

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.920
Well, I've completely lost this one.

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:59.930
Akitsuki Sho-kun, I should input that name.

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:05.180
<i>Akitsuki will advance 
to Round 3, the semifinals!</i>

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:10.500
Congrats. Amazing as usual, Sho.

00:18:10.990 --> 00:18:11.890
Tanaka.

00:18:11.890 --> 00:18:12.690
Huh?

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:15.360
I will make it to the finals.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.700
So, you make sure you come, too.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:21.490
You say, "come," but... 
I'm not a competitor—

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:24.190
I know you're a free surfer, Tanaka.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.740
But... I'll be waiting.

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:33.680
I see.

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:36.060
Well then, I guess I'll have to play 
out there with everything I've got.

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:37.370
See you in the finals.

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:43.760
In the finals.

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:47.660
<i>That the two of them had 
made such a promise...</i>

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:49.990
<i>I wasn't aware of it at the time, but...</i>

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.480
<i>Tanaka moved through 
to Round 3, the semifinals.</i>

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:02.190
What technique!

00:19:02.190 --> 00:19:05.530
It's like Miruru's rival... Kiraru!

00:19:05.530 --> 00:19:06.800
A formidable enemy.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:09.390
<i>Sho beat Naoya.</i>

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:21.910
<i>Tanaka, coming right down 
to the wire on time,</i>

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:24.070
<i>turns things around to win!</i>

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:28.640
That was close.

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:33.150
Tanaka-kun, was it?

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:36.150
You beat me.

00:19:37.180 --> 00:19:38.480
It was fun.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:41.150
It was a good game. Thank you.

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.590
What do you think?

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:55.300
The surfers in Oarai 
are impressive, aren't they?

00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:57.170
Yes. I was surprised.

00:19:57.170 --> 00:20:00.610
When you invited me, Bill-kun, 
I wasn't particularly inclined to do it,

00:20:00.610 --> 00:20:02.680
but I am glad I came.

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:05.380
In particular, Hinaoka Masaki-kun.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:09.180
Apparently, it's only been a year 
since he started surfing.

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:12.710
With that sense of balance, 
he's going to get a lot of attention.

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:14.390
Yes.

00:20:14.390 --> 00:20:16.250
His future looks promising.

00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:25.190
<i>I didn't get anywhere in the repechage, 
where the defeated compete for another chance.</i>

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:27.280
<i>The ones who advanced to the finals were...</i>

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:32.220
<i>The Forest Cup in Oarai Sun Beach.</i>

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:36.300
<i>In the final round we have Akitsuki Sho...</i>

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:42.760
Sho-kun!

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:44.130
Sho-sama!

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:45.740
Sho-sama!

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:49.810
Ready, and... Sho-kun!

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:52.230
The show must go on!

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:58.080
<i>And Tanaka Nalu.</i>

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:04.240
Tanaka-kun, you do your best out there, too!

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.910
While I'm at it, I'll cheer for you, too!

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:08.450
Nalu-sama!

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:14.420
Tanaka-kun, do your best out there, too!

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:18.990
They said I'm an add-on.

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:23.260
<i>And now, we'll begin the finals! 
The time limit is 30 minutes.</i>

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:25.260
Should we do this?

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:26.340
Yeah.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:35.250
<i>The fact that I wasn't standing 
there... was so frustrating.</i>

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:43.810
<i>But at the same time, I was proud.</i>

00:21:44.330 --> 00:21:47.480
<i>Sho and Tanaka...</i>

00:21:47.480 --> 00:21:50.540
<i>For my two best friends 
to be battling it out...</i>

00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:52.540
<i>It was like a dream...</i>

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:54.040
<i>It set a fire in my heart.</i>

00:21:59.260 --> 00:22:02.680
Sho! Tanaka! Both of you, you can do it!

00:22:13.960 --> 00:22:17.330
<i>Start the heat!</i>

00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:54.070
Wasn't there a picture 
that was a little bit cooler?

00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:54.070
<b>I'm grateful, but...</b>

00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:54.070
I've never seen
 you be cool.

00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:54.070
<b>Masaki
